/-!
# Bivariant classes towards a field and Chow homology, unconditionally

Let `k` be a field and let `X` be a scheme locally of finite type over `k`. **Stacks 0FBW** says
that cap product with the fundamental class of the point,

  `A^p(X ⟶ Spec k) ⟶ CH_{-p}(X)`,   `c ↦ c ∩ [Spec k]`,

is an isomorphism for every `p ∈ ℤ`. The map is `Stacks.Chow.bivariantToBaseEval`; its
injectivity is `Stacks.Chow.bivariantToBaseEval_injective` and its surjectivity
`Stacks.Chow.bivariantToBaseEval_surjective`, both stated over a general base with the inputs of
the proof as hypotheses. This file discharges every one of those hypotheses for the base situation
`Stacks.Chow.fieldChowSituation k`, the spectrum of `k` with the zero dimension function, and the
Gysin system `Stacks.Chow.gysinSystemOfInvertible` of first Chern classes of invertible modules.

Three of the hypotheses are theorems elsewhere: Stacks 02S1 (`Stacks.Chow.flatPullbackDescends`),
Stacks 02S2 (`Stacks.Chow.properPushforwardDescends`) and the existence of the flat-pullback class
of Stacks 0B78 (`Stacks.Chow.exists_isBivariantFlatPullback_ofInvertible`); Stacks 0EPK is
`Stacks.Chow.bivariantProperPushforwardOfInvertible`. The remaining two are proved here.

* **The fundamental class of an integral scheme is a flat pullback.** An integral scheme `T`
  locally of finite type over `k` has relative dimension `r = dim T` over `k`, its fundamental
  class lives in degree `r` alone, and flat pullback of `[Spec k]` along `T ⟶ Spec k` is `[T]`,
  because the base has delta-dimension zero (Stacks 02R4 with Stacks 02NK).
* **Chow classes are generated by pushforwards of flat pullbacks of the point.** A class
  `α ∈ CH_{-p}(X)` is the class of a locally finite cycle `∑ nᵢ [Zᵢ]` with the `Zᵢ` integral of
  dimension `r = -p`. The coefficients are unbounded and the sum may be infinite, so finitely many
  generators of the form `g_*[W]` with `W` a disjoint union of distinct `Zᵢ` cannot reach it.
  Instead take `W⁺ = ∐ Zᵢ`, each `Zᵢ` repeated `max(nᵢ, 0)` times, and `W⁻` likewise with
  `max(-nᵢ, 0)` copies. The family of copies is still locally finite, so `W^± ⟶ X` is proper; each
  `W^±` is flat of relative dimension `r` over `k`, its fundamental class is the flat pullback of
  `[Spec k]`, and its pushforward to `X` counts the copies above each `Zᵢ`. Thus
  `α = g⁺_*[W⁺] - g⁻_*[W⁻]` is a difference of two generators.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Chow.bivariantToBaseEval_bijective_of_field` — **Stacks 0FBW**: the canonical map
  `A^p(X ⟶ Spec k) ⟶ CH_{-p}(X)` is bijective.
* `Stacks.Chow.bivariantToBaseEquivOfField` — **Stacks 0FBW**, as an isomorphism of groups.
* `Stacks.Chow.integralFundamentalClassIsFlatPullback_fieldChowSituation` — over a field the
  fundamental class of an integral scheme is the flat pullback of the class of the point.
* `Stacks.Chow.chowClassesGeneratedByBaseFlatPullbacks_fieldChowSituation` — over a field Chow
  homology is generated by proper pushforwards of flat pullbacks of the class of the point.
* `Stacks.Chow.flatPullbackBaseClass_eq_fundamentalChowClass` — over a field the flat pullback of
  the class of the point along a flat `W ⟶ Spec k` of relative dimension `r` is `[W]_r`.
* `Stacks.Chow.properPushforward_fundamentalCycle_sigma_apply` — the pushforward of the
  fundamental cycle of a coproduct `∐ Zⱼ` of integral schemes along closed immersions `Zⱼ ⟶ X`
  has, at a point `y`, the number of summands with generic point over `y` as coefficient.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeDimension.of_sigmaι_comp` — a morphism out of a coproduct has
  relative dimension `d` once each summand does.

## Implementation notes

The base is `Stacks.Chow.fieldChowSituation k` rather than a general base whose scheme is the
spectrum of a field: the dimension function is part of the base situation, and only for the zero
dimension function is the fundamental class of an integral `T` in degree `dim T`, which is the
degree in which `Stacks.Chow.IntegralFundamentalClassIsFlatPullback` asks for it. For a constant
dimension function `c ≠ 0` that statement fails, `[Spec k]` then being zero in degree `0`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FBW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FBW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EPK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EPK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02R4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02R4)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02NK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02NK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02UC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02UC)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- A morphism out of a coproduct of schemes has relative dimension `d` (Stacks 02NJ) as soon as
its restriction to every summand does: the local dimension of a fibre at a point is computed on
the open summand containing it. -/
theorem RelativeDimension.of_sigmaι_comp {I : Type u} (Z : I → Scheme.{u}) {S : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : (∐ Z : Scheme.{u}) ⟶ S) [LocallyOfFiniteType f] {d : ℕ}
    (h : ∀ i, RelativeDimension (Sigma.ι Z i ≫ f) d) : RelativeDimension f d := by
  rw [relativeDimension_iff_forall_topologicalKrullDimAt]
  intro x
  obtain ⟨i, z, rfl⟩ := Stacks.Chow.exists_mem_range_sigmaι Z x
  rw [← fiberDimensionAt_comp_openImmersion (Sigma.ι Z i) f z]
  exact (relativeDimension_iff_forall_topologicalKrullDimAt _ d).1 (h i) z

end AlgebraicGeometry

namespace Stacks.Chow

/-- Repeating each member of a locally finite family finitely often gives a locally finite
family. -/
theorem locallyFinite_sigma_fst {X : Type*} [TopologicalSpace X] {ι : Type*} {β : ι → Type*}
    [∀ i, Finite (β i)] {f : ι → Set X} (hf : LocallyFinite f) :
    LocallyFinite fun j : (Σ i, β i) ↦ f j.1 := by
  intro x
  obtain ⟨U, hU, hfin⟩ := hf x
  exact ⟨U, hU, (hfin.sigma fun i _ ↦ Set.finite_univ (α := β i)).subset
    fun j hj ↦ ⟨hj, trivial⟩⟩

/-- Counting the elements of `Σ i, β i` whose first coordinate lies over `ι i`, for `ι`
injective, gives the cardinality of `β i`. -/
theorem finsum_mem_preimage_sigma_fst_one {X : Type*} {I : Type*} {β : I → Type*}
    [∀ i, Fintype (β i)] (ι : I → X) (hι : Function.Injective ι) (i : I) :
    ∑ᶠ j ∈ (fun j : (Σ i, β i) ↦ ι j.1) ⁻¹' {ι i}, (1 : ℤ) = Fintype.card (β i) := by
  have hset : (fun j : (Σ i, β i) ↦ ι j.1) ⁻¹' {ι i} = Set.range (Sigma.mk (β := β) i) := by
    ext ⟨l, m⟩
    simp only [Set.mem_preimage, Set.mem_singleton_iff, Set.mem_range]
    constructor
    · intro hl
      obtain rfl : l = i := hι hl
      exact ⟨m, rfl⟩
    · rintro ⟨m', ⟨⟩⟩
      rfl
  rw [hset, finsum_mem_range sigma_mk_injective, finsum_eq_sum_of_fintype]
  simp

section Coproduct

variable (C : ChowSituation.{u}) {X : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType sX]
  {J : Type u} (Zs : J → Scheme.{u}) [∀ j, IsIntegral (Zs j)] (v : ∀ j, Zs j ⟶ X)
  [∀ j, IsClosedImmersion (v j)] [IsProper (Sigma.desc v)] (π : J → X)
  (hπ : ∀ j, (v j).base (genericPoint (Zs j)) = π j) (n : ℤ)
  (hn : ∀ j, relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction sX (π j) = n)

include hπ hn in
/-- The generic point of a summand `Zⱼ` of `∐ Zⱼ ⟶ X` has the delta-dimension of its image in
`X`. -/
theorem relativeDimension_sigmaι_genericPoint (j : J) :
    relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction (Sigma.ι Zs j ≫ Sigma.desc v ≫ sX)
      (genericPoint (Zs j)) = n := by
  rw [← Category.assoc, Sigma.ι_desc, relativeDimension_comp_closedImmersion, hπ, hn]

open Classical in
include hπ hn in
/-- The fundamental cycle of a coproduct `∐ Zⱼ` of integral schemes all of delta-dimension `n` has
coefficient one at the generic point of each summand and zero elsewhere. -/
theorem fundamentalCycle_sigma_apply (j : J) (z : Zs j) :
    (fundamentalCycle C (Sigma.desc v ≫ sX) n).1 (Sigma.ι Zs j z) =
      if z = genericPoint (Zs j) then 1 else 0 := by
  classical
  have hgen := relativeDimension_sigmaι_genericPoint C sX Zs v π hπ n hn
  have hW : schemeDeltaDimension C (𝟙 (∐ Zs : Scheme.{u}) ≫ Sigma.desc v ≫ sX) ≤ (n : EInt) := by
    refine schemeDeltaDimension_le_of_forall_relativeDimension_le C _ _ fun w ↦ ?_
    obtain ⟨i, y, rfl⟩ := exists_mem_range_sigmaι Zs w
    have hZ : schemeDeltaDimension C (𝟙 (Zs i) ≫ Sigma.ι Zs i ≫ Sigma.desc v ≫ sX) ≤
        (n : EInt) := by
      rw [schemeDeltaDimension_eq_genericPoint, relativeDimension_comp_closedImmersion]
      simpa using (hgen i).le
    have h1 := relativeDimension_le_of_schemeDeltaDimension_le C _ (𝟙 (Zs i)) hZ y
    rw [relativeDimension_comp_isOpenImmersion] at h1
    simpa using h1
  have h := cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_apply_of_isOpenImmersion C C
    (Sigma.ι Zs j ≫ Sigma.desc v ≫ sX) (Sigma.desc v ≫ sX) (Sigma.ι Zs j)
    (𝟙 (∐ Zs : Scheme.{u})) (𝟙 (Zs j)) (Sigma.ι Zs j) (by simp) (by simp) n hW
    (fun x ↦ relativeDimension_comp_isOpenImmersion _ _ _ x) z
  change (fundamentalCycle C _ n).1 z = (fundamentalCycle C _ n).1 _ at h
  rw [← h, fundamentalCycle_eq_single C _ genericPoints_eq_singleton (hgen j)
    (Field.toIsField _)]
  simp [Function.locallyFinsuppWithin.single_apply]

include hπ hn in
/-- **The pushforward of the fundamental cycle of a coproduct.** Let `vⱼ : Zⱼ ⟶ X` be closed
immersions of integral schemes whose generic points map to points `π j` of delta-dimension `n`,
with `∐ Zⱼ ⟶ X` proper. The pushforward of `[∐ Zⱼ]_n` to `X` has at `y` the coefficient
`#{j | π j = y}`: each summand is mapped isomorphically onto its image near its generic point,
so it contributes its multiplicity, which is one. -/
theorem properPushforward_fundamentalCycle_sigma_apply (y : X) :
    (properPushforward C (Sigma.desc v ≫ sX) sX (Sigma.desc v) rfl n
      (fundamentalCycle C (Sigma.desc v ≫ sX) n)).1 y = ∑ᶠ j ∈ π ⁻¹' {y}, (1 : ℤ) := by
  classical
  have : SurjectiveOnStalks (Sigma.desc v) := surjectiveOnStalks_sigmaDesc Zs v
  have hres : ∀ x : (∐ Zs : Scheme.{u}),
      Function.Bijective (((Sigma.desc v).residueFieldMap x).hom) := fun x ↦
    bijective_residueFieldMap_of_surjective_stalkMap (Sigma.desc v) x
      ((Sigma.desc v).stalkMap_surjective x)
  set c := (fundamentalCycle C (Sigma.desc v ≫ sX) n).1 with hcdef
  have hterm : ∀ x : (∐ Zs : Scheme.{u}), c x *
      (if relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction (Sigma.desc v ≫ sX) x =
          relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction sX ((Sigma.desc v).base x)
        then ((Sigma.desc v).residueDegree x : ℤ) else 0) = c x := fun x ↦ by
    rw [relativeDimension_comp_of_bijective_residueFieldMap C.dimensionFunction _ sX x (hres x),
      residueDegree_eq_one_of_bijective_residueFieldMap _ x (hres x)]
    simp
  rw [properPushforward_apply, finsum_mem_congr rfl fun x _ ↦ hterm x]
  set e : J → (∐ Zs : Scheme.{u}) := fun j ↦ Sigma.ι Zs j (genericPoint (Zs j)) with hedef
  have he : Function.Injective e := fun j l hjl ↦ by
    by_contra hne
    exact Set.disjoint_left.mp (pairwise_disjoint_range_sigmaι Zs hne) ⟨_, rfl⟩
      (hjl ▸ ⟨_, rfl⟩ : e j ∈ Set.range (Sigma.ι Zs l))
  have hge : ∀ j, (Sigma.desc v).base (e j) = π j := fun j ↦ by
    rw [hedef, ← Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, Sigma.ι_desc, hπ]
  have hce : ∀ j, c (e j) = 1 := fun j ↦ by
    rw [hcdef, hedef, fundamentalCycle_sigma_apply C sX Zs v π hπ n hn, if_pos rfl]
  have hsupp : ∀ x, c x ≠ 0 → x ∈ Set.range e := fun x hx ↦ by
    obtain ⟨j, z, rfl⟩ := exists_mem_range_sigmaι Zs x
    rw [hcdef, fundamentalCycle_sigma_apply C sX Zs v π hπ n hn] at hx
    by_cases hz : z = genericPoint (Zs j)
    · exact ⟨j, by rw [hedef, hz]⟩
    · simp [hz] at hx
  calc ∑ᶠ x ∈ (Sigma.desc v).base ⁻¹' {y}, c x = ∑ᶠ x ∈ e '' (π ⁻¹' {y}), c x := by
        refine finsum_mem_inter_support_eq c _ _ (Set.ext fun x ↦ ?_)
        refine ⟨fun ⟨hx, hcx⟩ ↦ ⟨?_, hcx⟩, fun ⟨hx, hcx⟩ ↦ ⟨?_, hcx⟩⟩
        · obtain ⟨j, rfl⟩ := hsupp x hcx
          exact ⟨j, by simpa [hge] using hx, rfl⟩
        · obtain ⟨j, hj, rfl⟩ := hx
          simpa [hge] using hj
    _ = ∑ᶠ j ∈ π ⁻¹' {y}, c (e j) := finsum_mem_image he.injOn
    _ = ∑ᶠ j ∈ π ⁻¹' {y}, (1 : ℤ) := finsum_mem_congr rfl fun j _ ↦ hce j

end Coproduct

section Field

variable (k : Type u) [Field k]

/-- The spectrum of a field has delta-dimension zero over itself. -/
theorem schemeDeltaDimension_fieldChowSituation_base :
    schemeDeltaDimension (fieldChowSituation k)
      (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation k).S ≫ 𝟙 (fieldChowSituation k).S) ≤ ((0 : ℤ) : EInt) :=
  schemeDeltaDimension_le_of_forall_relativeDimension_le (fieldChowSituation k) _ _ fun w ↦ by
    rw [relativeDimension_id, fieldChowSituation_dimensionFunction]

/-- Over a field the fundamental class of an integral scheme `T` locally of finite type is
concentrated in degree `r = dim T`, `T ⟶ Spec k` has relative dimension `r`, and `[T]` is the
flat pullback of `[Spec k]` (Stacks 02NK, Stacks 02R4). -/
theorem integralFundamentalClassIsFlatPullback_fieldChowSituation
    (hS1 : FlatPullbackDescends (fieldChowSituation k)) :
    IntegralFundamentalClassIsFlatPullback (fieldChowSituation k) hS1 := by
  intro T sT _ _ sS _ hsS v _ hv
  subst hsS
  have hd := relativeDimension_of_isIntegral_over_field k v
  have hnn := relativeDimension_fieldChowSituation_nonneg k v (genericPoint T)
  have hsT : relativeDimension (fieldChowSituation k).dimensionFunction sT (genericPoint T) =
      ((relativeDimension (fieldChowSituation k).dimensionFunction v
        (genericPoint T)).toNat : ℤ) := by
    rw [← hv, Category.comp_id, Int.toNat_of_nonneg hnn]
  refine ⟨_, hd, fun j hj ↦ ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [fundamentalChowClass, fundamentalCycle_eq_zero_of_ne _ sT genericPoints_eq_singleton
      (by rw [hsT, zero_add] at *; exact fun h ↦ hj h.symm), map_zero]
  · exact (flatPullbackChow_fundamentalChowClass _ sT _ v hv _ hd 0 _
      (by simpa using schemeDeltaDimension_fieldChowSituation_base k)).symm

/-- Over a field a cycle in positive codimension `p`, i.e. of dimension `-p < 0`, is zero. -/
theorem cycleGroup_fieldChowSituation_eq_zero_of_pos {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (sX : X ⟶ (fieldChowSituation k).S) [LocallyOfFiniteType sX] {p : ℤ} (hp : 0 < p)
    (a : CycleGroup (fieldChowSituation k) sX (-p)) : a = 0 := by
  refine Subtype.ext (Function.locallyFinsuppWithin.ext fun x ↦ ?_)
  by_contra hx
  have h1 := (mem_cyclesOfDimension_iff_forall_point _ sX (-p) a.1).1 a.2 x hx
  have h2 := relativeDimension_fieldChowSituation_nonneg k sX x
  omega

open Classical in
/-- Over a field, let `a` be a cycle of dimension `r` on `X` and `M` a multiplicity on its
support. The coproduct `W` of `M i` copies of the integral component at each `i` maps properly to
`X`, is flat of relative dimension `r` over `k`, and the pushforward of `[W]_r` is `∑ M i [i]`. -/
theorem exists_properPushforward_fundamentalCycle_eq_multiplicity {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (sX : X ⟶ (fieldChowSituation k).S) [LocallyOfFiniteType sX] (r : ℕ)
    (a : CycleGroup (fieldChowSituation k) sX (-(-(r : ℤ))))
    (M : Function.support (a.1 : X → ℤ) → ℕ) :
    ∃ (W : Scheme.{u}) (g : W ⟶ X) (_ : IsProper g) (_ : LocallyOfFiniteType (g ≫ sX))
      (_ : Flat (g ≫ sX)) (_ : AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeDimension (g ≫ sX) r),
      ∀ y, (properPushforward (fieldChowSituation k) (g ≫ sX) sX g rfl (-(-(r : ℤ)))
        (fundamentalCycle (fieldChowSituation k) (g ≫ sX) (-(-(r : ℤ))))).1 y =
          if h : y ∈ Function.support (a.1 : X → ℤ) then (M ⟨y, h⟩ : ℤ) else 0 := by
  let Zs : (Σ i : ↥(Function.support (a.1 : X → ℤ)), Fin (M i)) → Scheme.{u} :=
    fun j ↦ (integralComponentAt (j.1 : X)).subscheme
  have : ∀ j, IsIntegral (Zs j) := fun j ↦ isIntegral_integralComponentAt _
  let v : ∀ j, Zs j ⟶ X := fun j ↦ (integralComponentAt (j.1 : X)).subschemeι
  have hlf : LocallyFinite fun j ↦ Set.range (v j) :=
    locallyFinite_sigma_fst (locallyFinite_range_subschemeι_support _ sX _ a)
  have : IsProper (Sigma.desc v) := isProper_sigmaDesc_of_locallyFinite Zs v hlf
  have hπ : ∀ j, (v j).base (genericPoint (Zs j)) = (j.1 : X) := fun j ↦
    genericPointOf_integralComponentAt _
  have hn : ∀ j : (Σ i : ↥(Function.support (a.1 : X → ℤ)), Fin (M i)),
      relativeDimension (fieldChowSituation k).dimensionFunction sX (j.1 : X) =
        -(-(r : ℤ)) := fun j ↦
    (mem_cyclesOfDimension_iff_forall_point _ sX _ a.1).1 a.2 _ j.1.2
  have hr : AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeDimension (Sigma.desc v ≫ sX) r :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeDimension.of_sigmaι_comp Zs _ fun j ↦ by
      have h := relativeDimension_of_isIntegral_over_field k (Sigma.ι Zs j ≫ Sigma.desc v ≫ sX)
      have e : (relativeDimension (fieldChowSituation k).dimensionFunction
          (Sigma.ι Zs j ≫ Sigma.desc v ≫ sX) (genericPoint (Zs j))).toNat = r := by
        rw [relativeDimension_sigmaι_genericPoint (fieldChowSituation k) sX Zs v
          (fun j ↦ (j.1 : X)) hπ _ hn j, neg_neg, Int.toNat_natCast]
      rwa [e] at h
  refine ⟨_, Sigma.desc v, inferInstance, inferInstance, inferInstance, hr, fun y ↦ ?_⟩
  rw [properPushforward_fundamentalCycle_sigma_apply (fieldChowSituation k) sX Zs v
    (fun j ↦ (j.1 : X)) hπ _ hn y]
  by_cases hy : y ∈ Function.support (a.1 : X → ℤ)
  · rw [dif_pos hy]
    exact (finsum_mem_preimage_sigma_fst_one
      (fun i : ↥(Function.support (a.1 : X → ℤ)) ↦ (i : X)) Subtype.val_injective
      ⟨y, hy⟩).trans (by simp)
  · rw [dif_neg hy]
    refine (finsum_mem_congr (Set.eq_empty_of_forall_notMem fun j hj ↦ hy ?_)
      fun _ _ ↦ rfl).trans finsum_mem_empty
    exact (show (j.1 : X) = y from hj) ▸ j.1.2

/-- Over a field every Chow class is a difference of two proper pushforwards of flat pullbacks of
the class of the point.

Write the class as that of a locally finite cycle `∑ nᵢ [Zᵢ]` (Stacks 02UC). In negative degree
there is nothing to do, every cycle being zero. Otherwise the pushforward of the fundamental
class of the coproduct of `max(nᵢ, 0)` copies of each `Zᵢ` has coefficient `max(nᵢ, 0)` at `Zᵢ`,
by `Stacks.Chow.properPushforward_fundamentalCycle_sigma_apply`, and that fundamental class is
the flat pullback of `[Spec k]` by
`Stacks.Chow.flatPullbackBaseClass_eq_fundamentalChowClass`; likewise with `max(-nᵢ, 0)`. -/
theorem chowClassesGeneratedByBaseFlatPullbacks_fieldChowSituation
    (hS1 : FlatPullbackDescends (fieldChowSituation k))
    (hpp : ProperPushforwardDescends (fieldChowSituation k)) :
    ChowClassesGeneratedByBaseFlatPullbacks (fieldChowSituation k) hS1 hpp := by
  classical
  intro X sX _ p α
  induction α using QuotientAddGroup.induction_on with
  | H a =>
    by_cases hp : 0 < p
    · rw [cycleGroup_fieldChowSituation_eq_zero_of_pos k sX hp a, QuotientAddGroup.mk_zero]
      exact zero_mem _
    obtain ⟨r, rfl⟩ : ∃ r : ℕ, p = -(r : ℤ) := ⟨(-p).toNat, by omega⟩
    have hgen : ∀ M : ↥(Function.support (a.1 : X → ℤ)) → ℕ,
        ∃ P : CycleGroup (fieldChowSituation k) sX (-(-(r : ℤ))),
          (P : chowGroup (fieldChowSituation k) sX (-(-(r : ℤ)))) ∈
            {β : chowGroup (fieldChowSituation k) sX (-(-(r : ℤ))) |
              ∃ (W : Scheme.{u}) (g : W ⟶ X) (hgp : IsProper g)
                (hgt : LocallyOfFiniteType (g ≫ sX)) (hgf : Flat (g ≫ sX)) (r' : ℕ)
                (hr : AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeDimension (g ≫ sX) r'), -(r' : ℤ) = -(r : ℤ) ∧
                let := hgp
                let := hgt
                let := hgf
                β ≍ properChowPushforward (fieldChowSituation k) (g ≫ sX) sX g rfl
                  (-(-(r' : ℤ))) (hpp _ _ g rfl _)
                  (flatPullbackBaseClass (fieldChowSituation k) (g ≫ sX) r' hr hS1)} ∧
          ∀ y, P.1 y = if h : y ∈ Function.support (a.1 : X → ℤ) then (M ⟨y, h⟩ : ℤ) else 0 := by
      intro M
      obtain ⟨W, g, hgp, hgt, hgf, hr, hP⟩ :=
        exists_properPushforward_fundamentalCycle_eq_multiplicity k sX r a M
      refine ⟨_, ⟨W, g, hgp, hgt, hgf, r, hr, rfl, heq_of_eq ?_⟩, hP⟩
      rw [flatPullbackBaseClass_eq_fundamentalChowClass]
      rfl
    obtain ⟨P, hP, hPy⟩ := hgen fun i ↦ (a.1 i).toNat
    obtain ⟨N, hN, hNy⟩ := hgen fun i ↦ (-a.1 i).toNat
    have hsub : a = P - N := by
      refine Subtype.ext (Function.locallyFinsuppWithin.ext fun y ↦ ?_)
      show a.1 y = P.1 y - N.1 y
      rw [hPy, hNy]
      split_ifs with h
      · simp only
        omega
      · simpa using h
    rw [hsub, QuotientAddGroup.mk_sub]
    exact sub_mem (AddSubgroup.subset_closure hP) (AddSubgroup.subset_closure hN)

variable {k} {X : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ (fieldChowSituation k).S) [LocallyOfFiniteType sX] (p : ℤ)

/-- **Stacks 0FBW.** Let `X` be locally of finite type over a field `k`. Cap product with the
fundamental class of the point, `A^p(X ⟶ Spec k) ⟶ CH_{-p}(X)`, is bijective. -/
@[stacks 0FBW "the bivariant classes are those of the Gysin system of invertible modules, \
`Stacks.Chow.gysinSystemOfInvertible`"]
theorem bivariantToBaseEval_bijective_of_field :
    Function.Bijective (bivariantToBaseEval (fieldChowSituation k)
      (gysinSystemOfInvertible (fieldChowSituation k)) sX p) :=
  bivariantToBaseEval_bijective_of_isBivariantFlatPullback _ _ sX p (flatPullbackDescends _)
    (integralFundamentalClassIsFlatPullback_fieldChowSituation k (flatPullbackDescends _))
    (properPushforwardDescends _)
    (fun sW _ _ r hr ↦ exists_isBivariantFlatPullback_ofInvertible _ sW r hr)
    (bivariantProperPushforwardExistsOfInvertible _)
    (chowClassesGeneratedByBaseFlatPullbacks_fieldChowSituation k (flatPullbackDescends _)
      (properPushforwardDescends _))

/-- **Stacks 0FBW.** For `X` locally of finite type over a field `k`, the identification
`A^p(X ⟶ Spec k) ≃ CH_{-p}(X)`, `c ↦ c ∩ [Spec k]`, as an isomorphism of groups. -/
@[stacks 0FBW "the bivariant classes are those of the Gysin system of invertible modules, \
`Stacks.Chow.gysinSystemOfInvertible`"]
def bivariantToBaseEquivOfField :
    bivariantToBase (fieldChowSituation k) (gysinSystemOfInvertible (fieldChowSituation k)) sX p ≃+
      chowGroup (fieldChowSituation k) sX (-p) :=
  AddEquiv.ofBijective _ (bivariantToBaseEval_bijective_of_field sX p)

/-- The identification of Stacks 0FBW is cap product with the class of the point. -/
@[simp]
theorem bivariantToBaseEquivOfField_apply
    (c : bivariantToBase (fieldChowSituation k) (gysinSystemOfInvertible (fieldChowSituation k))
      sX p) :
    bivariantToBaseEquivOfField sX p c =
      bivariantToBaseEval (fieldChowSituation k) (gysinSystemOfInvertible (fieldChowSituation k))
        sX p c :=
  rfl

end Field

